.TH lrm 1 "@PROJECT_YEAR@" "@PROJECT_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lrm \- manage and benchmark Linux distribution package mirrors
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lrm
.RI [ OPTION ]...
.IR COMMAND
.RI [ ARGS ]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lrm
stores mirror aliases and URLs, benchmarks them with ping or HTTP download
tests, and applies the selected mirror to the local package manager
configuration. Supported distribution families are detected from
.BR /etc/os-release :
Debian/Ubuntu (apt), RHEL-family (dnf/yum), and Arch (pacman).
.PP
Mirror definitions are stored under
.RI $XDG_CONFIG_HOME /repoman/lrm/ .
On the first run, when that file does not exist yet,
.B lrm
creates it with built-in default mirrors for the detected distribution family
(Debian, RPM, or Arch), including public mirrors such as 163 and Aliyun where
available.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Increase logging verbosity. May be repeated
.RB ( \-vv ", " \-vvv ", " \-vvvv ) :
level 1 logs per-mirror tests,
level 2 logs paths and privilege elevation,
level 3 logs measurements and commands,
level 4 logs external tool output.
When standard error is a terminal and terminfo is available, log lines are
colored by level (green progress, cyan/blue/magenta/dim verbosity, yellow
warnings, red errors).
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Reduce logging verbosity.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit successfully.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version information and exit successfully.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
List configured mirrors as
.IR MARK " [" N "] " ALIAS .
.RB MARK
is
.BR * " (selected), " \- " (failed last test), " ? " (untested), or two spaces.
.RB N
is a one-based shortcut accepted by
.BR use " and " remove .
With
.BR \-p " or " \-\-priority ,
also print priority and URL.
.TP
.BR add " [[" \- PRIORITY "] | " \-p ", " \-\-priority " " N "] " ALIAS URL
Add or update a mirror. Optional priority is written as
.BR \- N
before the alias or with
.BR \-p
(default 100; lower is preferred in listings).
.TP
.BR remove " " ALIAS\|NUM
Remove a mirror by alias or list number.
.TP
.BR use " [" \-c ", " \-\-config\-only "] [" apply opts "] " ALIAS\|NUM
Set the default mirror and apply it to the system package manager.
.PP
Debian apply options (default
.BR \-\-all ):
.BR main ", " contrib ", " non-free ", " non-free-firmware
components,
.BR deb\-src ,
suite-updates, backports, and a security stanza.
Flags include
.BR \-a ", " \-\-all ", " \-s ", " \-\-src ", " \-u ", " \-\-updates ", " \-b ", " \-\-backports ", " \-\-security ", " \-\-suite .
.PP
RPM apply options (default BaseOS only):
.BR \-e ", " \-\-everything
enables BaseOS, AppStream, and CRB/PowerTools;
.BR \-E ", " \-\-epel
adds EPEL;
.BR \-a ", " \-\-all
enables everything plus EPEL.
Also
.BR \-\-releasever ", " \-\-arch ", " \-\-appstream ", " \-\-crb ", " \-\-powertools ", " \-\-minimal .
The same apply options are accepted by
.BR pingsel " and " bwsel .
.PP
Use
.B \-\-config\-only
to write
.I /etc/apt/sources.list.d/lrm.sources
without running
.BR apt\-get " update".
Use a list number (e.g.
.B 3
) or alias (e.g.
.BR tuna ).
.TP
.BR pingtest " [" \-n ", " \-\-count " " N "] [" \-W ", " \-\-timeout " " SEC "]"
Ping each mirror host in parallel and print mirrors sorted by latency and
packet loss (default count 3, timeout 2 seconds).
.TP
.BR bwtest " [" \-\-ref " " BYTES "]"
Download a repository metadata file from each mirror in parallel using
.BR getbar (1)
and print mirrors sorted by score. Each test runs
.RB getbar " -c -d2 -p1 -w3 -s30m -i.1 -q"
on the mirror probe URL. Score is the effective bytes per second to download a
3 MiB reference file:
.RI ref / ( offset + ref/bps ) ,
so connection delay matters more for fast mirrors and less when the transfer
itself is slow. A declining linear fit
.RI ( \-p
slope) reduces the score if throughput drops before the reference size is
reached. Override the reference size with
.BR \-\-ref
or
.IR LRM_BWTEST_REF_BYTES .
.TP
.BR pingsel " [" apply opts "] [" \-n ", " \-\-count " " N "] [" \-W ", " \-\-timeout " " SEC "]"
Run
.B pingtest
and apply the best mirror (same apply options as
.BR use ).
.TP
.BR bwsel " [" apply opts "] [" \-\-ref " " BYTES "]"
Run
.B bwtest
and apply the best mirror (same apply options as
.BR use ).
.TP
.B help
Show usage.
.TP
.B version
Show version.
.SH INTERNATIONALIZATION
User-visible messages use gettext (text domain
.BR lrm ).
Message catalogs are searched under the source
.I po/
tree, the build tree, then the installed locale directory.
Set
.BR LANGUAGE ", " LC_ALL ", or " LANG
to select a translation (e.g.
.BR zh_CN ).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/repoman/lrm/mirrors
Tab-separated mirror database:
.IR alias ", " priority ", " url .
.TP
.I ~/.config/repoman/lrm/default
Currently selected mirror alias.
.TP
.I ~/.config/repoman/lrm/health
Last ping/bwtest result per mirror (
.BR ok " or " bad ).
.TP
.I /etc/apt/sources.list.d/lrm.sources
Applied Debian/Ubuntu mirror (deb822 format).
.TP
.I /etc/yum.repos.d/lrm.repo
Applied RPM-family mirror.
.TP
.I /etc/pacman.d/mirrorlist
Applied Arch mirror list.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Add mirrors and list them:
.B lrm add -10 tuna https://mirrors.tuna.tsinghua.edu.cn/debian
.br
.B lrm add ustc https://mirrors.ustc.edu.cn/debian
.br
.B lrm list
.TP
Benchmark and select the fastest:
.B lrm bwsel
